course: dictionary
lesson: 974
title: Blurt out
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To blurt means to say something suddenly, without thinking first. The words come out before you can stop them, and they are often something you should have kept secret. The usual phrase is blurt out.
explain: «Many traditions treat a lie blurted out in panic differently from a planned deception.» Blurted out in panic means the lie came out fast and was not planned. The clues are panic, which means sudden fear, and planned, which is the opposite of blurted.
explain: Try the swap test. Put «said suddenly, without thinking» in place of blurted out, and the sentence still makes sense. In class, blurting out an answer means calling it out without putting your hand up first.
fact: To blurt means to say something suddenly, without thinking first.
fact: Blurt out is the usual phrase, as in blurt out an answer or blurt out a secret.
fact: «Blurted out in panic» shows the words came out fast, with no planning.
fact: Blurting out answers in class means calling out without putting your hand up.
fact: A blurt often gives away a secret that you meant to keep.
exercise: Ella was keeping the surprise party a secret, but she blurted out the news at breakfast. What does blurted mean? | Sang it softly to herself | Wrote it down carefully | Asked a question politely | *Said suddenly, without thinking first
exercise: Sam blurted out the answer before the teacher had finished her question. What did Sam do? | Whispered it to a friend | Waited patiently for a turn | *Said it suddenly, without waiting | Wrote it on the board
exercise: Mum says, «Don't blurt out the secret!» What is she asking you to do? | *Keep it in, and think before you speak | Write it on a sign | Shout it to the whole street | Tell it twice to be sure
test: «She blurted out her secret before she could stop herself.» What does blurted out mean? | Said very slowly and carefully | Hid under the bed | *Said suddenly, without thinking | Forgot completely
test: Which phrase is the best swap for blurt out in «He blurted out the answer»? | Asked nicely for a turn | Drew a picture of it | Thought about it for a long time | *Said out suddenly, without thinking first
exam: How can you check the meaning of blurt in a sentence? | *Swap in said suddenly without thinking and see if the sentence still makes sense | Count the letters in the word | Look only at the first letter | Find a word that rhymes with it
